rule: CORE-DUMP-1, FE-TR-1, FE-TR-3
In full Core the lambda is closure-converted (a label, no captures, a closed
body) and the let has no type. With the Prelude imported, an integer literal
is its fromInteger, which Idris evaluates while elaborating only below 100:
here 100 is still a call, which idr-eval folds (mlir.check). putStrLn is the
Prelude's; its instance, its erased arguments and the literals are left
unchecked.
CHECK: Main.main : PrimIO.IO[Builtin.Unit] =
CHECK-NEXT: let w = \lam{{[0-9]+}}[](w Int) => add_Int(#0, {{.+}})
CHECK-NEXT: Prelude.IO.putStrLn{{.*}}cast_IntString((#0 (#0 {{.+}}))))
